From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxjivi05 <maxjividen@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Relocate DLLs before their section protections are set.

A DLL without IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_DYNAMIC_BASE whose preferred base
is taken gets mapped somewhere else and is relocated on the PE side by
perform_relocations(): every section is switched to PAGE_READWRITE, the
fixups are applied, and the old protection is put back.

Under the WOW64 FEX translator with DEP disabled for the process (as for
any executable built without IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_NX_COMPAT), the
read-write step marks the code pages as executable and writable. Putting
PAGE_EXECUTE_READ back does not clear that state, so the translator keeps
them read-only for code invalidation and VirtualQuery() reports
PAGE_READONLY on .text. A hooking library that checks the target is
executable before patching it then refuses, and the program fails to
start.

The unix side already relocates dynamically based images while the view
is still writable, before the section protections are set. Do the same
for any relocatable DLL that did not land at its preferred base, and
update ImageBase so perform_relocations() has nothing left to do and no
protection change is needed. Executables, images with stripped
relocations and images without a relocation directory keep the existing
path.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3496,15 +3496,24 @@ static NTSTATUS map_image_into_view( struct file_view *view, const UNICODE_STRIN
 
     /* relocate to dynamic base */
 
-    if (image_info->map_addr && (delta = image_info->map_addr - image_info->base))
+    if (image_info->map_addr)
+        delta = image_info->map_addr - image_info->base;
+    else if ((image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_DLL) &&
+             !(image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_RELOCS_STRIPPED) &&
+             get_data_dir( nt, total_size, IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_BASERELOC ))
+        delta = (ULONG_PTR)ptr - image_info->base;
+    else
+        delta = 0;
+
+    if (delta)
     {
-        TRACE_(module)( "relocating %s dynamic base %lx -> %lx mapped at %p\n", debugstr_us(nt_name),
-                        (ULONG_PTR)image_info->base, (ULONG_PTR)image_info->map_addr, ptr );
+        TRACE_(module)( "relocating %s base %lx -> %lx mapped at %p\n", debugstr_us(nt_name),
+                        (ULONG_PTR)image_info->base, (ULONG_PTR)(image_info->base + delta), ptr );
 
         if (nt->OptionalHeader.Magic == IMAGE_NT_OPTIONAL_HDR64_MAGIC)
-            ((IMAGE_NT_HEADERS64 *)nt)->OptionalHeader.ImageBase = image_info->map_addr;
+            ((IMAGE_NT_HEADERS64 *)nt)->OptionalHeader.ImageBase = image_info->base + delta;
         else
-            ((IMAGE_NT_HEADERS32 *)nt)->OptionalHeader.ImageBase = image_info->map_addr;
+            ((IMAGE_NT_HEADERS32 *)nt)->OptionalHeader.ImageBase = image_info->base + delta;
 
         if ((dir = get_data_dir( nt, total_size, IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_BASERELOC )))
         {
